how do you stay motivated when you're  starting a business it's a great  question that came in from a YouTube  viewer Yee boys fully boyish full wrote  in my question is how do you stay  motivated when starting a business and  things are not working out especially  when you have a young family to feed  welcome to the club you know what most  people can't get their business beyond  that startup phase where they're  actually making a nice income for  themselves the way to do it the way to  stay motivated  three things gonna give you three advice  this is goal write it down save it  the first is believe in what you're  doing you have to have a bigger goal a  bigger vision a bigger purpose for what  you're doing with your business and that  can fuel you most businesses shut down  not because it wasn't a great idea but  because the entrepreneur gives up too  soon they don't allow time for momentum  to grow into build and some of the  greatest entrepreneurs were failures  like you look at George Lucas started  star wars multi-billionaire his first  six years and his business was a failure  he thought he should go back and get a  job and be practical and listen to his  friends advice he kept going because he  loved what he was doing and he had a  strong belief and passionate it was the  right thing to do you have to find that  with your business it's the most  important thing if you are not there if  you're doing a business just to make  money stop stop right now it's not going  to work go for something that you  passionately believe in and let that  passion fuel you wake up knowing this is  the mission that you are on you are  gonna help people with this specific  problem that can help you it's not the  whole answer because it's still hard  getting up every day even when you  passionately believe in what you're  doing  some days are a lot better than others  okay the next thing that really helped  me was I looked at famous entrepreneurs  I looked up to people who I respected  who I admired and saw that these guys  struggled to like George Lucas and I  think if these guys struggled then I'm I  could be like them too  you know it's not just me it's not like  everybody else's was an overnight  success and I'm the loser who can't  figure it out everybody has a hard time  and I read the stories of people who are  respected who are looked up to for  people who are inside my industry and  outside my industry I've got ideas from  them  I got specific strategies from them but  I also just got motivation from them  when I saw how hard it was for them to  get going and to make this thing work  nobody has that overnight success they  all struggle to get this thing to go so  that gave me extra encouragement  motivation I would start by reading a  story in the morning and it gave me a  little bit of fuel that's why I started  my business my website with the largest  collection of famous entrepreneur  profiles online because I needed that  for my business I needed that to help me  stay inspired and stay motivated and it  still inspires and motivates me and I  wanted to share that with other people  that's why I launched the company so  look to you what I call aspirational  Mentors and get their guidance wisdom  and momentum to help put back into your  business the third thing that really  helped me was customer feedback so when  you see that you're really helping  somebody and you're changing their lives  that should be fuel for you and you may  not be you know making it big yet but  those little stories help keep you going  I remember for me in the early days of  starting this business I've been  Carmical calm I would do events and  webinars and seminars and meet  entrepreneurs and I remember that day  after that the seminar I felt great I  felt wow I just changed these people's  lives they were heading down the wrong  path I I saved them I'm helping to build  a way better business I felt so good  about myself when you help somebody you  feel great and I love I love what I was  doing I felt like this is right like how  could I ever doubt it what I was doing  this is fantastic and then the next day  I wake up and it's gone that feeling of  empowerment excitement is gone I don't  know why you fall asleep you wake up the  next day it's just gone and was hard to  get out of bed so what I did that helped  me was I saved some of the comments that  came back  I saved some of the special emails that  came back  where people write in to say Evan you  changed my life thank you so much please  keep going I can't wait for your next  event and I read those whenever I felt  down whenever I felt low in energy I  read those and they picked me up and  made me realize that you know what what  I'm doing really matters and even if  it's only hitting a few people right now  it matters it's changing people's lives  it's helping them I need to keep going  and that gave me the motivation the  inspiration to just go another day  another day another day you keep  pounding it out so those are the three  things right remember why you're doing  this what your big passion big belief is  look to aspirational mentors people who  you look up to respect and see what they  did and just get their story and plant  it in your head and remember that they  didn't have an easy time either and  three look to your customer feedback see  that you are helping them and change in  the world changing their lives and use  that to feel you to keep going where are  you out right now I feel for you you  know you've got a young family you're  trying to feed them you want to keep  going you want to believe in your dream  and not go back and get a job working  for somebody that you hate you know  doing work that's way beneath you not  living up to your potential and at the  same time you got a balance hey I got  bills to pay I got to put food on the  table these people are depending on me  I'm going to feel guilty if I don't  deliver for them hopefully your family  is supportive of you doing this  initiative but the best thing to think  about right now is I want you to have  that big dream it's great have the big  goal but for now get to survival like  what's a smaller version of that big  dream that gets you to the point of  survival what do you need to make a  month so just to get by I'm not talking  glamorous lifestyle we're not talking  Ferraris and Porsches here I'm talking  like gas money lunch money that's what  you need to survive so you don't go back  and get a job what does that look like  and how can you get there as fast as  possible  that's your first criteria is getting to  survival whatever it takes to get there  and it's not going to be your ideal  company but it makes sure that you are  in business so you don't have to quit go  back get a job and watch some  but he else make huge dollars off of  your idea so figure out what that number  is what you need to survive I need X  thousand dollars a month to survive and  figure out your plan just to get there  while keeping your big goal your big  vision in mind once you get to survival  things can really take off for you  that's your opportunity to blow it up  but you have to get to that point first  believe for those of you watching please  give it a thumbs up below makes me want  to do more for you and I want to hear  what you have to say  leave a comment underneath let me know  if you liked the video or not if you  have a question put it in the comments  I'll make a video response for you thank  you guys I love you we'll see you soon  you
 

